  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Hunters in the middle",
  "description": "Mark out an area of about 20 × 15 metres with cones. Every player has a ball and lines up on one short side, except one or two who put their ball aside and stand in the middle. They are the hunters.\n\nOn the signal everyone with a ball dribbles across to the other side. The hunters try to kick as many balls as they can out of the area. A player who loses the ball fetches it, puts it aside and becomes a hunter too. Then everyone dribbles back, and so on until only one or a few still have their ball. They win the round and start as hunters in the next one.\n\nVariant: play until everyone has lost their ball, and start with more players in the middle so that everyone gets a turn as a hunter. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Keep the ball close to your foot when a hunter comes – small touches."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Look up and dribble into the free space, away from the hunters."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Put your body between the hunter and the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Hunters: work together and cut off the same player."
    }
  ],
